      "observed": "In the pH and EC sensor blocks, the ADM3260 isolated-side SDA/SCL pins and the non-isolated-side SDA/SCL pins are both labeled NET0095/NET0071, and the GNDISO pins are tied to the global GND symbol.",
      "expected": "The specification requires each EZO circuit to be behind a galvanically isolated I2C bridge with separate isolated I2C nets and isolated grounds (/SDA_pH, /SCL_pH, /SDA_EC, /SCL_EC, /GNDISO_pH, /GNDISO_EC).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U5/U2 ADM3260: SDA1/SCL1 and SDA2/SCL2 both show NET0095/NET0071; GNDISO pins connect to GND (sheet 1, pH/EC sensor blocks)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Two Atlas Scientific EZO circuits (pH, EC) each sit behind a dedicated 2.5 kV galvanically-isolated I2C bridge ... isolated ground (/GNDISO_pH, /GNDISO_EC)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The pH/EC isolation is bypassed; the wet-probe I2C lines and grounds are merged with the digital domain, defeating the intended galvanic isolation and exposing the board to ground loops/noise and possible damage.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
