      "nets": ["NET0057"],
      "observed": "NET0057 connects the ADM3260 PDIS pins to the TMC2209 PD/UART pins, merging the EZO power-disable control with the stepper-driver UART bus.",
      "expected": "The specification separates EZO_PDIS (tied to IO6/SPI_CLK) from the shared single-wire UART bus STEP_BUS used by the TMC2209 drivers.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U5/U2 pin 8 PDIS and U4/U11/U8 UART pins are labeled NET0057 (sheet 1, pH/EC and peristaltic pump driver blocks)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "An EZO_PDIS net ties both U3 pin 8 and U4 pin 8 ... to a single ESP32 pin (IO6/SPI_CLK) ... shared single-wire UART bus (STEP_BUS)"}
      ],
      "impact": "Power-disabling the pH/EC isolators would disturb the TMC2209 UART bus, and UART traffic would toggle the isolator PDIS pins; the intended independent control of the isolators and stepper drivers is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["PR2", "H6", "P7"],
      "pins": ["PR2.VCC", "PR2.SCL", "PR2.SDA", "PR2.GND"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0095", "NET0071", "GND"],
      "observed": "The LiDAR water-height sensor PR2 is wired to +5V and the main I2C labels NET0095/NET0071.",
      "expected": "The specification states the TF-Luna LiDAR is present in the BOM but not wired: its pins are free and it is excluded from the board; the wired water-level sensing is an ultrasonic sensor on two GPIOs.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Water Height Sensor: PR2 LiDAR connected to +5V, NET0095, NET0071, GND (sheet 1, water level sensor block)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "its pins are \"free\" and it is marked on_board: no ... it is not connected to any net in this design"}
      ],
      "impact": "An unsupported 5V/I2C LiDAR device is added to the bus, potentially causing address/current conflicts, while the intended ultrasonic water-level sensing path is not implemented.",
      "confidence": 0.70
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic deviates from the intended design in several ways: the pH/EC isolators are bypassed by shared I2C/GND nets, the EZO power-disable net is merged with the TMC2209 UART bus, and the LiDAR is wired despite being specified as not connected."
}

